On-demand engines for filee-cli.

Upstream Filee now ships `filee engines` (list, install, download, remove), but `convert` and `watch` still fail
when an optional engine is missing instead of installing it, and macOS still has no FFmpeg or Ghostscript download.
This patch:

 * installs the engines a conversion needs before it runs (`convert`, and per batch in `watch`), with `--no-install`
   to turn that off. Uses `CliHost.Engines` (`EngineInstaller`) so downloads, SHA-256 verification, mirrors and
   per-package locking match `filee engines install`. Progress and messages go to stderr (suppressed in `--quiet`
   and `--json` so stdout stays one JSON document and stderr stays JSON events only). Empty files never trigger a
   download.
 * adds the two engines upstream does not offer on macOS to engines.json: FFmpeg (Martin Riedl's release build, kind
   `zip-programs` with ffprobe as a companion file) and Ghostscript (conda-forge's gs, kind `conda-unix`), and the two
   install kinds that unpack them (including companion support for `SaveFilesAsync` / `InstallFromFilesAsync` /
   `DownloadSize`). Every download is checked against its SHA-256 before it is unpacked.
 * tests for the new install kinds, companions, and path safety, and guards `Zip_to_iso` when 7-Zip is not fetched
   (same as `Folder_to_zip`).

Drop each piece when upstream ships an equivalent.

